-- title:
--   Hecke characters realising narrow ray class characters
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\mathfrak{f}$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $\chi$ be a group homomorphism from the narrow ray class group of $K$ modulo $\mathfrak{f}$ — that is, from the quotient of the group of units of fractional ideals whose valuation count at every height-one prime dividing $\mathfrak{f}$ vanishes, by the subgroup generated by the set `narrowRaySet` of $K$ and $\mathfrak{f}$ — to $\mathbb{C}^\times$. Then there is a homomorphism $\eta$ from the group of units of the adele ring of $K$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ with the following four properties. First, $\eta$ is a finite-order Hecke character: it is trivial on the image of $K^\times$ under the diagonal embedding, it is continuous, and it is of finite order. Second, $\eta$ admits $\mathfrak{f}$ as modulus: $\eta(u) = 1$ for every idele unit $u$ whose archimedean component is $1$ and whose component at each height-one prime $v$ has valuation $1$ and satisfies $v(u_v - 1) \le \exp(-n_v)$, where $n_v$ is the multiplicity of $v$ in the factorisation of $\mathfrak{f}$. Third, $\eta$ is unitary: $\lVert \eta(x) \rVert = 1$ for all $x$. Fourth, for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with $v \nmid \mathfrak{f}$, the value of $\eta$ at the idele which is $1$ at the archimedean places and at all finite places other than $v$, and at $v$ is the image of a chosen uniformizer of $v$, equals $\chi$ of the class of the fractional ideal $v$.
--
--   This is the existence direction of the classical dictionary between characters of narrow ray class groups and finite-order Hecke characters of the idele class group with prescribed conductor bound, in the form needed to pass from ideal-theoretic to adelic data. It is used in the construction of ray class character twists of automorphic forms and in the comparison of ray symbols with products of local values of finite-order Hecke characters.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LT_HeckeChar_exists_heckeCharOfRayClassChar.lean

import Definitions.Def_NarrowRayClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_HeckeCharacter_FiniteOrder
import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi
import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_HeckeEigenfunction

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem LT.HeckeChar.exists_heckeCharOfRayClassChar
    (K : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (𝔣 : Ideal (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
    (χ : Deep.NTSupply.NarrowRayClassGroup K 𝔣 →* ℂˣ) :
    ∃ η : (NumberField.AdeleRing (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K) K)ˣ →* ℂˣ,
      HeckeCharacter.IsFiniteOrderHeckeChar K η ∧
      HeckeCharacter.AdmitsModulus K η 𝔣 ∧
      AutomorphicForm.IsUnitaryChar (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K) K η ∧
      ∀ (v : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (NumberField.RingOfIntegers K))
        (hv : ¬ v.asIdeal ∣ 𝔣),
        η (AutomorphicForm.uniformizerIdele K v)
          = χ (Deep.NTSupply.primeClass K 𝔣 v hv) := by sorry
